    "fact_rationales": {
      "F11": "The positive immunohistochemistry results for CD31, CD34, and Ki-67 (<1%) are more typical of Kaposi's sarcoma (FLAT.1) and bacillary angiomatosis (FLAT.2).",
      "F12": "The negative immunohistochemistry results for podoplanin (D2-40) and human herpesvirus 8 (HHV-8) are more characteristic of conditions other than Kaposi's sarcoma (FLAT.1) and bacillary angiomatosis (FLAT.2).",
      "F7": "The presence of multiple firm, nonscaly, purple erythematous patches and plaques with irregular borders is more typical of angioma (FLAT.3) than other candidates.",
      "F9": "The histopathological examination showing thin-walled, irregularly branched blood vessels dispersed between thickened collagen bundles is more characteristic of angioma (FLAT.3) and bacillary angiomatosis (FLAT.2)."
